# Additive functors preserve direct sums
%%%
tag := "Chapter7/Discussion_after_Definition7.9.1"
number := false
%%%

It is easy to show that if $`F` is an additive functor, then $`F(X \oplus Y)` is canonically isomorphic to $`F(X) \oplus F(Y)`.
